From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:58:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm-shim/panfrost: answer the GET_PARAMs the kmod layer
 requires

pan_kmod's panfrost backend queries L2_FEATURES, SELECTED_COHERENCY and
others with required=true, so the noop shim aborted (assert in
panfrost_query_raw) before the device came up and rusticl could not be
used offline. Return 0 for the feature words that have no bearing on the
shim (coherency, barrier size, timestamps, priorities), 1 core group, and
let PAN_SHADER_PRESENT override the core mask so an MP1 part such as the
Mali-G31 can be modelled (PAN_GPU_ID=7093 PAN_SHADER_PRESENT=1).

Host tooling only; used to compile OpenCL kernels with the real rusticl
pipeline on x86 and dump the Bifrost code.

Rebased onto Mesa 26.3: upstream now answers L2_FEATURES (0x7120306) itself, so that
param is left to upstream.

Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 src/panfrost/drm-shim/panfrost_noop.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/drm-shim/panfrost_noop.c b/src/panfrost/drm-shim/panfrost_noop.c
index a8f6481535c..261a76259bc 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/drm-shim/panfrost_noop.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/drm-shim/panfrost_noop.c
@@ -64,9 +64,23 @@ panfrost_ioctl_get_param(int fd, unsigned long request, void *arg)
       return 0;
    }
 
-   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_SHADER_PRESENT:
-      /* Assume an MP4 GPU */
-      gp->value = 0xF;
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_SHADER_PRESENT: {
+      /* Assume an MP4 GPU unless PAN_SHADER_PRESENT says otherwise */
+      const char *sp = os_get_option("PAN_SHADER_PRESENT");
+      gp->value = sp ? strtol(sp, NULL, 16) : 0xF;
+      return 0;
+   }
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_CORE_FEATURES:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_COHERENCY_FEATURES:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_SELECTED_COHERENCY:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_THREAD_MAX_BARRIER_SZ:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_SYSTEM_TIMESTAMP:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_SYSTEM_TIMESTAMP_FREQUENCY:
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_ALLOWED_JM_CTX_PRIORITIES:
+      gp->value = 0;
+      return 0;
+   case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_NR_CORE_GROUPS:
+      gp->value = 1;
       return 0;
    case DRM_PANFROST_PARAM_L2_FEATURES:
       gp->value = 0x7120306;
